 # Image lerp sandbox
 
+> **Not the production path any more.** Building an intermediate skin tone by mixing two
+> finished plates also mixes the garment, the shading, the specular and the two plates'
+> misregistration, and it changes the face. Production now interpolates the skin COLOUR
+> only and corrects the current plate's skin toward it, leaving everything else as
+> generated — see `liforma/tools/image-to-image/scripts/skin_target.py`. This sandbox
+> stays as the comparison arm and for eyeballing a raw mix; the same formula is ported
+> verbatim into `compare_skin_interpolation.py`.
+
 Client-side SvelteKit tool that loads two images and builds a third by linearly interpolating their pixels.
 
